al/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Commercial & HOA Claim Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/commercial-hoa-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Roof & Hail Damage Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/roof-hail-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Windstorm & Tornado Damage Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Ice Storm & Snow Load Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/ice-storm-snow-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Water Damage Claim Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/water-damage-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Damage Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/house-fire-smoke-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wildfire Loss Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/wildfire-loss-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/fallen-tree-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance Estimate Review","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/carrier-estimate-review/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/property-appraisals/neutral-umpire-services/"}}]},"knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Property claim valuation","Wildfire claims","Ice storm damage","Windstorm damage"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}],"priceRange":"$$"},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Oregon Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#webpage","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/","name":"Oregon Insurance Appraisal FAQ | Costs, Timing & Rules","description":"Oregon insurance appraisal FAQ, grouped by topic: how appraisal works, what it costs, deadlines, Oregon rules and working with us.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-17","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#primaryimage","url":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/living-room.webp","width":960,"height":640},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#faq"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Questions answered","item":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/"}],"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is insurance appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A process in most property policies for settling disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an agreement signed by two of the three sets the amount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is appraisal the same as arbitration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not exactly. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal. It doesn’t decide coverage or legal claims."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I demand appraisal if my claim was denied?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Appraisal is designed for disputes about the amount of a covered loss. If the claim was denied outright, you will generally need to resolve coverage first, usually with an attorney."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does my Oregon policy have an appraisal clause?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most homeowner and commercial property policies do. Look in the conditions section for a paragraph titled “Appraisal.” Oregon’s standard fire-policy provisions also include an appraisal process."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays for appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each side usually pays its own appraiser, and the umpire’s fee is usually split equally. Check your policy’s wording."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do appraisers charge?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Flat fees, hourly rates or a percentage of the increase are all common. We put our fee in writing before any work starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the first conversation free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We will look at what you have and tell you honestly whether appraisal is likely to help."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does appraisal take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Simple residential claims often finish within two to three months of both appraisers being named. Large or complex claims take longer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a deadline to demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some policies set one; many don’t. But the policy’s deadline to file a lawsuit, commonly two years from the loss in Oregon, keeps running. Talk to an attorney if it is near."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to name my appraiser quickly?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many clauses give each side about 20 days after a written demand to name an appraiser. Check yours."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who regulates insurers in Oregon?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Division of Financial Regulation, part of the Oregon Department of Consumer and Business Services. It licenses insurers, agents and public adjusters and accepts consumer complaints."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I file a complaint and use appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A complaint with the Division of Financial Regulation addresses claim handling; appraisal addresses the amount of loss. They can run side by side."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Oregon FAIR Plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Oregon FAIR Plan Association offers basic property coverage to owners who can’t find it in the regular market. Its policies have their own terms, including appraisal provisions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Oregon have special wildfire rules?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"After the 2020 Labor Day fires, Oregon adopted additional protections for wildfire policyholders in some situations, such as more time to collect replacement cost after a total loss in a declared emergency. Confirm current rules with the Division of Financial Regulation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is earthquake damage covered?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not by a standard homeowner policy. Earthquake coverage is usually an endorsement or separate policy with a percentage deductible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal and don’t give legal advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you work outside the Portland area?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We work statewide across all 36 counties."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I send for a first review?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The insurer’s estimate, your contractor’s estimate, photos, the declarations page and any letters from the insurer."}}],"@id":"https://oregoninsuranceappraiser.com/claim-questions-oregon/#faq"}]}</script>
</head>
